<Window x:Class="NextRdp.Desktop.HelpWindow"
        xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        Title="NextRDP help" Width="720" Height="650" MinWidth="620" MinHeight="500"
        WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner" ShowInTaskbar="False"
        Background="{DynamicResource AppBackground}" Foreground="{DynamicResource PrimaryText}">
    <Grid Margin="24">
        <Grid.RowDefinitions><RowDefinition Height="*"/><RowDefinition Height="Auto"/></Grid.RowDefinitions>
        <FlowDocumentScrollViewer VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto" IsToolBarVisible="False" ScrollViewer.PanningMode="VerticalFirst">
            <FlowDocument Background="Transparent" Foreground="{DynamicResource PrimaryText}" FontFamily="Segoe UI Variable Text, Segoe UI" FontSize="14">
                <Paragraph FontSize="24" FontWeight="SemiBold">NextRDP quick guide</Paragraph>
                <Paragraph Foreground="{DynamicResource SecondaryText}">NextRDP keeps connection metadata on this computer and lets the Microsoft Windows RDP client request credentials for every session. NextRDP does not save passwords.</Paragraph>
                <Paragraph FontSize="18" FontWeight="SemiBold">Connections and folders</Paragraph>
                <List>
                    <ListItem><Paragraph>Use <Bold>New connection</Bold> to set the target, folder, tags, environment, username hint, notes, and RDP redirection controls.</Paragraph></ListItem>
                    <ListItem><Paragraph>Double-click a saved connection or press Enter in the connection list to open it in a tab.</Paragraph></ListItem>
                    <ListItem><Paragraph>Use <Bold>Full screen</Bold> after the session connects. The pinned Microsoft RDP connection bar provides Restore and Minimize controls; Ctrl+Alt+Break also returns to the windowed session.</Paragraph></ListItem>
                    <ListItem><Paragraph>Favorites and Recent are built-in views. Selecting a folder includes connections in its nested folders.</Paragraph></ListItem>
                </List>
                <Paragraph FontSize="18" FontWeight="SemiBold">Import safety</Paragraph>
                <Paragraph>Imports accept .rdp and RDCMan .rdg files up to 2 MB. An .rdg import may contain at most 2,000 servers, 32 folder levels, and 64 XML element levels. Unsafe folder names and deeper hierarchies are rejected before saving. Password blobs, credential fields, secrets, and tokens are removed before the review screen. Existing host/port pairs are shown as duplicates and remain unselected.</Paragraph>
                <Paragraph FontSize="18" FontWeight="SemiBold">Diagnostics</Paragraph>
                <Paragraph>Diagnostics resolve every available IPv4/IPv6 address and try the configured TCP port within a five-second total timeout. Successful TCP access does not prove that credentials or RDP policy will be accepted.</Paragraph>
                <Paragraph FontSize="18" FontWeight="SemiBold">Keyboard shortcuts</Paragraph>
                <Table CellSpacing="0">
                    <TableRowGroup>
                        <TableRow><TableCell><Paragraph><Bold>Ctrl+N</Bold></Paragraph></TableCell><TableCell><Paragraph>New connection</Paragraph></TableCell></TableRow>
                        <TableRow><TableCell><Paragraph><Bold>Ctrl+E</Bold></Paragraph></TableCell><TableCell><Paragraph>Edit selected connection</Paragraph></TableCell></TableRow>
                        <TableRow><TableCell><Paragraph><Bold>Ctrl+K</Bold></Paragraph></TableCell><TableCell><Paragraph>Focus global search</Paragraph></TableCell></TableRow>
                        <TableRow><TableCell><Paragraph><Bold>Ctrl+D</Bold></Paragraph></TableCell><TableCell><Paragraph>Toggle favorite</Paragraph></TableCell></TableRow>
                        <TableRow><TableCell><Paragraph><Bold>Enter</Bold></Paragraph></TableCell><TableCell><Paragraph>Connect from the connection list</Paragraph></TableCell></TableRow>
                    </TableRowGroup>
                </Table>
                <Paragraph FontSize="18" FontWeight="SemiBold">Production safety</Paragraph>
                <Paragraph>Production connections use a red environment marker, require an explicit warning confirmation, and keep a red border around the session. The per-connection production watermark is enabled by default and can be turned off in the connection editor.</Paragraph>
                <Paragraph FontSize="18" FontWeight="SemiBold">High Contrast</Paragraph>
                <Paragraph>NextRDP follows the Windows High Contrast setting automatically and uses Windows system colours. The decorative Production watermark is hidden in High Contrast while the Production confirmation and session indicator remain available.</Paragraph>
            </FlowDocument>
        </FlowDocumentScrollViewer>
        <Button Grid.Row="1" Content="Close" IsCancel="True" HorizontalAlignment="Right" MinWidth="100" Margin="0,16,0,0"/>
    </Grid>
</Window>
